@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
' purpose: the decision space around deleting the docker+egress backend and keeping mitmproxy as observability only
' would touch: internal/backend/dockeregress/** (the backend that would be deleted)
' would touch: internal/egress/**, internal/egressproxy/**, cmd/proveo-egress/**
' would touch: internal/reviewgate/**, internal/ptyproxy/**
' would touch: internal/provider/provider.go (the ACL field, once nothing consumes it)
' would touch: internal/run/run.go (buildPosture's EgressTier), internal/backend/sandbox/sandbox.go
' session: b2e065e3-98e9-4974-ae9e-86990b8b1c81
' PLANNED. _spec/_plans/ is exempt from the SPEC-reference rule — nothing here
' is cited from source because nothing here has landed. This file states a
' DECISION SPACE. Every measured fact is marked MEASURED; everything else is a
' QUESTION and is written as one. No option below is chosen.
'
'   what kept this backend alive  _spec/_paradigms/retire-dind.puml (APPLIED)
'   what waits on deleting it ... _spec/_plans/secret-custody.puml (item d)
'   the escape hatch's own plan . _spec/_plans/host-execution-fallback.puml
'   the observability half ...... _spec/internal/egressproxy/mitm-and-flow-record.puml
'   the tiers at stake .......... _spec/internal/egress/egress-tiers.puml
'   the consent flow at stake ... _spec/internal/reviewgate/pty-review-proxy.puml
'   what enforces on sbx ........ _spec/internal/sbx/policy-baseline.puml
'   the boundary being restated . _spec/_paradigms/egress-boundary.puml
'   the credential half ......... _spec/_paradigms/credential-boundary.puml
' Notes are capped at 5 lines x 50 columns; one idea per anchor.
'
' ── THE PROPOSAL, STATED ONCE AND NOT ARGUED FOR ───────────────────────────
' Delete the docker+egress backend. sbx becomes the only sandbox. mitmproxy
' survives ONLY as an observability tool — the flow recorder — and never again
' as an enforcement hop. That is the operator's proposal. This plan records it,
' records what is measurably true around it, and then asks what it costs. It
' does not accept it.
'
' ── WHAT IS ALREADY TRUE — MEASURED ────────────────────────────────────────
' 1. THERE ARE TWO ENFORCEMENT MODELS, NOT ONE WITH A SWITCH.
'    docker+egress: a mitm proxy chained to Squid, governed by proveo's own
'    tiers `open` / `allowlist` / `review` (internal/egress).
'    sbx: NO proveo proxy at all. `posture.EnforcedBy(true)` prints
'    "sbx — Kit network allowlist + credential proxy (proveo runs no Squid or
'    MITM)". The run log says it in those words.
'
' 2. retire-dind DELIBERATELY KEPT THIS BACKEND. Its SCOPE section says the
'    fate of mitmproxy and Squid is "deliberately NOT decided here — they serve
'    the docker backend, which survives this change as the PROVEO_SBX=0
'    fallback". That plan is APPLIED; this one is the decision it declined.
'
' 3. secret-custody (d) IS BLOCKED ON EXACTLY THIS. Its ledger reads:
'    "retire-dind landed and kept the docker backend, so (d) now waits on
'    deleting it". `WriteBrokerEnv` still writes `broker.env` on that path.
'    That plan now cross-references this file, so the dependency is no longer
'    pointing at a decision with no home.
'
' 4. THE OBSERVABILITY HALF IS ALREADY SPECIFIED AND ALREADY NARROW.
'    mitm-and-flow-record.puml documents flows.ndjson as host, method, path and
'    status, with NO query string, headers or body — the query is stripped
'    because the broker can inject a credential as `?key=`. That is the half
'    the proposal would keep, and it is already the safe half.
'
' ── THE FORCING EXAMPLE — A DEFECT MEASURED TODAY ──────────────────────────
' This is the clearest argument that having two models has a running cost, and
' it is recorded verbatim rather than paraphrased.
'
'   internal/backend/sandbox/sandbox.go:677 writes the Kit allowlist
'   UNCONDITIONALLY:
'       Permissions: sbx.KitPermissions{Network: sbx.KitNet{Allow: allow}}
'   where `allow` is built at ~490-503 from the def's `Capabilities.Hosts`
'   plus `credentials.ReachableHosts(in.Detected)`.
'   THE EGRESS TIER IS NEVER CONSULTED IN THAT PATH.
'
'   internal/run/run.go:487 sets the reported posture from
'       EgressTier: p.Mode
'   which is proveo's DOCKER-backend tier.
'
' So an sbx run PRINTS `egress tier: open` while WRITING a narrow allowlist
' that `open` cannot widen. An operator with an allow-all host baseline found
' `https://api.x.ai/v1/models/` blocked and reasonably expected "open" to mean
' open. `.x.ai` is in `internal/provider/provider.go` as both an ACL
' (`dstdomain .x.ai`) and a broker host — but it only enters the Kit allowlist
' if the run DETECTS an x.ai key, and no tier can add it.
'
' `WarnBaseline` (internal/backend/sandbox/sandbox.go:868) already half-admits
' this: "the tier below describes proveo's intent, not what sandboxd will
' enforce". But it fires ONLY when the global sbx baseline is allow-all, and it
' never says the tier is inert against the Kit allowlist. The half-admission is
' evidence of the split, not a fix for it.
'
' ── THE OPEN QUESTIONS. NONE OF THESE IS ANSWERED HERE ─────────────────────
' Q1. WHAT BECOMES OF THE TIER VOCABULARY? Does `open` / `allowlist` / `review`
'     survive as declared INTENT, mapped onto sbx's baseline plus the Kit
'     allowlist — or is it retired with the backend it describes? The x.ai case
'     forces the question either way: today the word and the enforcement
'     disagree, and both a mapping and a retirement would end that.
'
' Q2. WHERE DOES THE REVIEW GATE GO? `internal/reviewgate` and its consent flow
'     are built on the docker proxy chain — a CONNECT hook plus a pty proveo
'     owns (pty-review-proxy.puml). sbx has no equivalent hop. Is `review`
'     retired, reimplemented on some other seat, or deferred to the sandbox
'     vendor? retire-dind already noted it "stops being proveo's to give"; that
'     was an observation, not a decision.
'
' Q3. CAN MITM OBSERVE ON sbx AT ALL? sbx runs no proveo proxy. Keeping mitm as
'     observability means finding it a seat on a backend that has none — or
'     accepting that flow records become docker-only, which under this proposal
'     means gone. retire-dind's legend sketches ONE route (chain proveo's
'     inspector into sbx's own proxy via the Kit's `environment.variables`, with
'     `PROVEO_EGRESS_UPSTREAM` already existing) and lists its costs: proveo's
'     CA must be trusted inside the sandbox, sbx injects credentials at ITS
'     proxy so chain order matters, and the NO_PROXY-as-regex hazard is live.
'     Sketched is not chosen. Which is it: a seat, or no flow record?
'
' Q4. WHAT HAPPENS TO THE SQUID ACL VOCABULARY? `provider.Entry` carries BOTH
'     `ACL` (a `dstdomain …` body for Squid) and `Hosts` (broker inject/strip,
'     and what feeds the sbx Kit). If Squid goes, `ACL` has no consumer. Is it
'     deleted, or is it the only machine-readable statement of a provider's
'     domain set and therefore worth keeping under a different name? Deleting a
'     field is easy; deleting the only place a fact is written down is not.
'
' Q5. WHAT ACTUALLY UNBLOCKS secret-custody (d)? (d) is "a plaintext credential
'     in a mounted file". Deleting the backend removes the mounted-home shape.
'     Does it also remove `broker.env`, or does a surviving observability mitm
'     still need a credential from somewhere — moving the prerequisite a third
'     time rather than closing it? The answer decides whether (d) is unblocked
'     or merely re-pointed.
'
' Q6. WHAT IS THE MIGRATION SIGNAL FOR `PROVEO_SBX=0`? Today it selects a
'     different container. After this it selects something else entirely, and
'     what that something is has its own plan
'     (_spec/_plans/host-execution-fallback.puml). Does the variable warn and
'     no-op the way `PROVEO_DIND` does, hard-fail, or silently change meaning?
'     Silently is the one answer retire-dind already rejected once.
title PLANNED — retire docker+egress: what the second backend still holds, and what has nowhere to go

component "**docker+egress backend**\nwhat the proposal would delete" as DOCKER <<error>>

node "what lives inside it today" as INSIDE <<host>> {
  component "mitmproxy\nenforcement hop AND flow recorder" as MITM <<app>>
  component "Squid\n""dstdomain"" ACLs from provider.Entry" as SQUID <<app>>
  component "internal/reviewgate + ptyproxy\nCONNECT hook + a pty proveo owns" as REV <<app>>
  component "internal/egress tiers\nopen · allowlist · review" as TIERS <<app>>
}

component "sbx backend\nKit allowlist + sbx's own credential proxy" as SBX <<app>>
database "flows.ndjson\nhost · method · path · status" as FLOWS <<db>>
cloud "sbx's proxy — the only route out\n""gateway.docker.internal:3128""" as SBXPROXY <<cloud>>

component "**the defect**\nprinted tier vs written allowlist" as DEFECT <<error>>
component "secret-custody (d)\nplaintext credential in a mounted file" as CUSTODY <<error>>
component "provider.ACL\nno consumer once Squid goes" as ACL <<error>>
component "the PROVEO_SBX=0 escape hatch\nstops meaning: the other container" as ESCAPE <<error>>

DOCKER ARROW_MAIN INSIDE
TIERS ARROW_MAIN SQUID
TIERS ARROW_MAIN MITM
REV ARROW_MAIN MITM
MITM ARROW_QUEUE FLOWS
SQUID ARROW_MAIN ACL
DOCKER ARROW_ERROR SBX : deleted — but not replaced part for part
SBX ARROW_ERROR REV : no hop to ask on
SBX ARROW_ERROR FLOWS : no proveo proxy to record at
MITM ARROW_OPTIONAL SBXPROXY : Q3 — a seat, or nothing?
TIERS ARROW_ERROR DEFECT
SBX ARROW_ERROR DEFECT
DOCKER ARROW_ERROR CUSTODY : while it lives, (d) stays open
DOCKER ARROW_ERROR ESCAPE : see host-execution-fallback

note bottom of DEFECT
  **MEASURED. The tier never reaches the Kit.**
  ""sandbox.go:677"" writes the allowlist
  unconditionally from harness hosts plus
  reachable hosts. Nothing on that path reads
  the tier, so ""open"" cannot widen it.
end note

note top of DEFECT
  **MEASURED. The run says both things.**
  ""run.go:487"" reports ""EgressTier: p.Mode"" —
  the DOCKER tier — on an sbx run. Printed
  ""open"", enforced narrow. That is one
  vocabulary describing another's boundary.
end note

note bottom of DEFECT
  **The x.ai case is the forcing example.**
  An allow-all host baseline, tier ""open"", and
  ""api.x.ai/v1/models/"" blocked anyway: that
  domain enters the Kit only if a key is DETECTED.
  "Open" named an intent nobody enforced.
end note

note top of DEFECT
  **""WarnBaseline"" half-admits it already.**
  It says the tier "describes proveo's intent,
  not what sandboxd will enforce" — but only
  when the global baseline is allow-all, and
  never that the tier is inert. Evidence, not fix.
end note

note bottom of TIERS
  **Q1 — intent, or retirement?** Do
  open/allowlist/review survive as a declared
  intent mapped onto sbx's baseline and Kit, or
  go with the backend? Unanswered here. Both
  answers end the disagreement above.
end note

note bottom of REV
  **Q2 — where does consent live?** The gate
  needs a CONNECT hook and a pty proveo owns.
  sbx offers neither. Retired, reimplemented, or
  deferred to the vendor? retire-dind observed
  the problem; it did not decide it.
end note

note bottom of MITM
  **Q3 — can it observe on sbx at all?**
  Keeping mitm as observability needs a seat on
  a backend that runs no proveo proxy. Chaining
  into sbx's own proxy is SKETCHED in
  retire-dind, not chosen. Seat, or no record?
end note

note top of FLOWS
  **What would survive is already the safe
  half.** host, method, path, status — no
  query, no headers, no body, because the
  broker can inject ""?key="". Nothing about
  keeping this needs the enforcement hop.
end note

note bottom of ACL
  **Q4 — delete the field, or the fact?**
  ""provider.Entry"" carries ""ACL"" for Squid and
  ""Hosts"" for the broker and the Kit. If Squid
  goes, ""ACL"" has no reader — but it may be the
  only written-down form of a provider's domains.
end note

note bottom of CUSTODY
  **Q5 — unblocked, or moved again?**
  (d) waits on deleting this backend. Does
  deleting it also retire ""broker.env"", or does
  a surviving mitm still need a key from
  somewhere — a third move, not a close?
end note

note top of CUSTODY
  **The prerequisite has moved twice already.**
  First "retire the sidecar", then "delete the
  backend". A plan that moves it a third time
  should say so out loud rather than claim a
  close. This one claims nothing.
end note

note bottom of ESCAPE
  **Q6 — what does the operator see?**
  ""PROVEO_SBX=0"" today picks another container.
  After this it picks something categorically
  different. Warn-and-no-op, hard-fail, or
  silent? Silent was already rejected once.
end note

note top of SBX
  **This plan does not assume sbx is enough.**
  It is the only backend the proposal leaves.
  Whether that is a security win depends on the
  six answers above, not on the deletion — and
  none of them is settled in this file.
end note

legend bottom
  **What this plan is, and is not**
  ==
  **IS** — a record of one proposal, four measured facts, one measured defect, and six
  questions with no answers written into them.
  --
  **IS NOT** — a decision, a sequence of steps, or a design. There is deliberately no
  ordered plan here: an order implies the destination is chosen, and it is not.
  ==
  **The one thing this file DOES settle**: secret-custody's item (d) now cross-references
  a real path instead of an unnamed future decision, in both directions.
  --
  **The one thing it hands off**: what ""PROVEO_SBX=0"" would then mean is a separate and
  larger question, because the answer stops being "a container". See
  _spec/_plans/host-execution-fallback.puml.
end legend
@enduml
